{
  "dom_id": "step-q103998",
  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "$$\nf(t,z)=\u27e83\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t,\\,\\text{_____},\\,z\u27e9,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(t,z)$ above parametrizes one sheet of the hyperbolic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=9$ for $x\\ge 3.$ What is the second component of $f?$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that the hyperbola ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=9$ for $x\\ge 3$ in $xy$-plane has the parametrization\n\n$$\n\u27e8x,y\u27e9=\u27e83\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t,\\,3\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t\u27e9,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})\n$$\n\nsince \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =(3\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t)^{2}-(3\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t)^{2} \\\\  & =9({sec}^{2}\u2061t-{tan}^{2}\u2061t) \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t,z) & =\u27e8x,y,z\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t,\\,3\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t,\\,z\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the second component of $f$ is $3\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t.$",
